# SFR-write manifest — regenerated by audit_sfr_writes.py --update.
# Every entry: ADDR  PATTERN  IMMEDIATE  # source-file(s)
# Any diff between the current .rst set and this file fails the
# audit gate. Update ONLY after reviewing what changed and
# confirming the new write is intentional.
#
# Bug precedent — 2026-07-22 flash #2 was `USBCTL = 0xC0`
# (assign,0xc0) at 0xfffc when Rev 20 has (or,0x80). A baseline
# generated from a working image would have flagged that
# specific tuple as a diff before flash.
#
# NOTE: --update rewrites this file and DROPS per-entry annotations.
# The standing annotations are kept below the entry list instead, so a
# re-baseline cannot silently erase them.
#
# RE-BASELINED 2026-07-28 (second time today), 82 -> 80 entries, for the
# DMA-enable fix. Reviewed diff:
#   + 0xff67 / 0xff9f runtime (IEPBCTY1 / OEPBCTY2) — Rev 20 fcn.0x0728
#     @ 0x07EA and 0x07F2 clear both the X and Y buffer counts in the
#     streaming tail. We previously cleared X and then zeroed the buffer
#     SIZE registers instead of Y, which is not what Rev 20 does.
#   + 0xffe8 / 0xffee or 0x80, and_not 0x7f — DMAEN set/clear on the two
#     real DMA channel control registers. This is the fix: the firmware
#     had never once set DMAEN, so the capture endpoint buffer was never
#     filled and every isochronous IN packet came back zero-length.
#   - 0xff62 / 0xff9a runtime — the IEPBSIZ1 = 0 / OEPBSIZ2 = 0 writes
#     removed by the same change. The `assign 0x40` forms that program
#     the real buffer size remain.
#   - 0xffe5/e6/e7 and 0xfff7/f8/f9 assign 0x61,0xa8,0x0f — the dead
#     dma_program_48k() helper, deleted. It was never called, and its
#     name asserted a rate mapping the live code contradicts.

0xff2e  rmw       -       # usb
0xff60  assign    0x00    # streaming,usb
0xff60  assign    0xc5    # streaming
0xff61  assign    0x60    # streaming
0xff62  assign    0x40    # streaming
