# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Standing annotations (kept below the entries so `--update` can't drop
# them; the parser ignores comment lines wherever they appear).
#
# USBCTL (0xfffc) — three writes, all intentional and cited:
#   assign 0x00 (main.c): defensive disconnect at top of main(), and the
#     same write in the deferred enter-DFU path before the signature is
#     invalidated. POLICY §2 carve-out A. Matches Rev 20 disasm 0x08E5
#     (master init) and safety_net's top-of-main disconnect.
#   or 0x80 (usb.c): CONN alone at cold init — mirrors Rev 20 0x0AE2.
#   or 0xC0 (usb.c): RMW attach — CONN + FEN together. FEN required per
#     datasheet §6.5.1.4 ("UBM ignores all USB transactions" when FEN=0).
#     usb_init is called at boot and re-called from VEC_RSTR, so both
#     paths reliably set FEN. Rev 20 splits this the same way.
#
# USBIMSK (0xfffd) — 0xF5 = RSTR|SUSR|RESR|SOF|SETUP|STPOW (datasheet
#   §6.5.1.3: 7=RSTR 6=SUSR 5=RESR 4=SOF 3=PSOF 2=SETUP 1=rsvd 0=STPOW).
#   Was 0xE5, the same set without SOF, and telemetry block 5 measured
#   tlm_sof_count == 0 on hardware because of it. Rev 20 uses 0x9F, which
#   also enables SOF; we keep SUSR/RESR that Rev 20 omits, and still
#   leave PSOF masked.
#
# 0xffe8 / 0xffee are DMACTL0 / DMACTL1 (datasheet §6.5.2.3), the real
#   DMA channel control registers. 0xffe1 is ACGCTL, a clock-generator
#   register — it is NOT a DMA register, despite the name this repo used
#   for it until 2026-07-28. Writing 0xC0 to 0xffe1 does not arm any DMA
#   channel; DMAEN is bit 7 of 0xffe8/0xffee.
